# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must stay that way: this repo is a fork
# of a public upstream, so anything committed here is world-readable.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Resolution order for every key below is: real environment -> this file -> the collector's
# own .env at ../../alphaess-collector/.env. That last one only resolves for a checkout
# sitting beside alphaess-collector on a dev machine, which is why a Mac works today with
# no token here. It never resolves inside a container, so on the NAS this file (or
# docker-compose) is what supplies them.


# --- InfluxDB, fed by alphaess-collector -------------------------------------------------
# The planner refuses to run without SOC, so a missing token is a hard stop, not a warning.

# Where InfluxDB is. Use ONE of these two forms.
#   from a container on the NAS, over the shared docker network:
INFLUX_URL=http://influxdb:8086
#   from a laptop on the LAN, talking to the NAS directly (INFLUX_PORT defaults to 8086):
#INFLUX_HOST=192.168.68.105
#INFLUX_PORT=8086

# Needs read on the actuals bucket and write on the plan bucket:
#   read:alphaess + write:planning
INFLUX_TOKEN=

INFLUX_ORG=home

# Actuals written by the collector: SOC, load, PV.
INFLUX_BUCKET=alphaess

# Optional. Only needed if more than one AlphaESS system reports into the same bucket.
#ALPHAESS_SYS_SN=

# Sampling interval the collector runs at. Used to judge whether an hour is fully covered,
# so a collector outage is rejected instead of reading as a very quiet house.
#POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=30


# --- Container (docker-compose.yml only) --------------------------------------------------
# Ignored outside the container. The image runs as a non-root user whose UID must match the
# owner of ./data on the host, because a bind mount replaces the image's ownership with the
# host's. Get it wrong and nothing errors: Marstek-planning.py wraps its os.makedirs in a
# bare except, so every run silently refetches instead of caching, and the symptom that
# eventually shows up is forecast.solar rate-limiting. Check the host directory with:
#
#     mkdir -p data && ls -n | grep data
#
# then put those two numbers here and rebuild.
#PLANNER_UID=1000
#PLANNER_GID=1000


# --- KNMI ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not used by any code yet. Parked here for the PV-forecast work in NAS-DEPLOYMENT-PLAN.md
# ("A better PV forecast source"). Get one from dataplatform.knmi.nl:
#   API Catalog -> Open Data API -> "Request an API key". Shown once, so save it here.
#KNMI_API_KEY=
